cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "OrbitDrift"
abstract: ""Ephemeris staleness as a measured divergence curve against epoch age, scoped honestly as a lower bound because the product has no precision-ephemeris or TLE archive access — SGP4 self-consistency between user-supplied epochs as the practical proxy, numerical integration with declared J2-J4, drag and luni-solar perturbations as independent dynamics, learned error-growth predictor with calibrated intervals benchmarked against linear, quadratic and drag-dominated analytic growth forms on interval coverage and width; energy and angular-momentum conservation, integrator step-refinement convergence and SGP4 reproduced against its published test vectors. Must not present any output as a covariance for conjunction assessment.""
